<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1989</h1><p class="ref-lede">1989 in world history: 49 events, 20 deaths, 4 states founded and 4 that came to an end. 259 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1985">1985</a><a href="/years/1986">1986</a><a href="/years/1987">1987</a><a href="/years/1988">1988</a><a href="/years/1989" aria-current="page">1989</a><a href="/years/1990">1990</a><a href="/years/1991">1991</a><a href="/years/1992">1992</a><a href="/years/1993">1993</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Montreal Protocol to protect the ozone layer enters into force</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The treaty phasing out chlorofluorocarbons and other ozone-depleting chemicals came into effect. Ratified by every UN member, it is widely regarded as the most successful environmental agreement ever made.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-10">10 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ron Brown becomes the first Black chairman of a major US party</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ron Brown was elected chairman of the Democratic National Committee. He helped Bill Clinton win in 1992 and became Secretary of Commerce before dying in a plane crash in 1996.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-14">14 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ayatollah Khomeini issues a fatwa against Salman Rushdie</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>'s leader called on Muslims to kill the author of 'The Satanic Verses' and his publishers. Rushdie spent years in hiding; translators and publishers were attacked, and he was stabbed in 2022.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-12">12 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tim Berners-Lee proposes the World Wide Web</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cern">CERN</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>, Berners-Lee circulated 'Information Management: A Proposal' for a hypertext system linking documents across computers. His supervisor called it 'vague but exciting'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-15">15 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fatal crush at Hillsborough stadium in Sheffield</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A crush on the terraces at an FA Cup semi-final killed 97 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liverpool">Liverpool</a> supporters. Fresh inquests in 2016 found they were unlawfully killed and that fans bore no blame.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-30">30 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Students unveil the Goddess of Democracy in Tiananmen Square</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Art students erected a ten-metre statue facing Mao's portrait as a symbol of the pro-democracy movement. Troops destroyed it when they cleared the square on 4 June.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/beijing" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beijing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-3">3 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Chinese troops move on Tiananmen Square</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">On the night of 3 to 4 June, the army forced its way into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, firing on crowds. Hundreds, possibly thousands, were killed, ending seven weeks of pro-democracy protest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-3">3 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ayatollah Khomeini dies in Tehran</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini">Ruhollah Khomeini</a>, leader of the 1979 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-revolution">Iranian Revolution</a> and the Islamic Republic's first Supreme Leader, died aged 86. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-khamenei">Ali Khamenei</a> succeeded him the next day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-4">4 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Solidarity sweeps Poland's semi-free elections</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solidarity-polish-trade-union">Solidarity</a> won all but one of the freely contested seats. The result led to the first non-communist-led government in the Soviet bloc and began the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-europe">Eastern Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-europe">Eastern Europe</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-23">23 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Two million people form the Baltic Way human chain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some two million people joined hands across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvia">Latvia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> on the 50th anniversary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molotov-ribbentrop-pact">Nazi-Soviet Pact</a>. The 675 km chain demanded independence, regained in 1990-91.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-28">28 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ferdinand Marcos dies in exile in Hawaii</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Former Philippine president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos">Ferdinand Marcos</a> died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a>, three years after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/people-power-revolution">People Power Revolution</a> drove him from power. His regime was notorious for martial law and plunder.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-9">9 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Berlin Wall opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a confused announcement that East Germans could travel freely, crowds pressed the border crossings until guards opened the gates. The fall of the Wall led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-reunification">German reunification</a> within a year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/prague" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prague.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-17">17 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Police attack students in Prague, sparking the Velvet Revolution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Riot police beat students at a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> march marking the anniversary of a Nazi crackdown. Outrage fuelled mass protests that ended communist rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> within six weeks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-17">17 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Simpsons premieres as a series</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fox broadcast the first full episode of The Simpsons, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a> special. It became the longest-running American animated series and scripted primetime show.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-20">20 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The United States invades Panama</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">US forces launched <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-invasion-of-panama">Operation Just Cause</a> to remove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama">Panama</a>'s military ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a>, who was wanted in the US on drug trafficking charges. Noriega surrendered on 3 January 1990.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/revolutions-of-1989" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolutions-of-1989.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/revolutions-of-1989">Revolutions of 1989</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The revolutions of 1989 were the wave of largely peaceful uprisings that overthrew the communist regimes of Central and Eastern Europe.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre">1989 Tiananmen Square protests and massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 1989 Tiananmen Square protests were student-led demonstrations in Beijing and other Chinese cities from April to June 1989, calling for political reform, freedom of the press and an end to corruption.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/caracazo" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caracazo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/caracazo">Caracazo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Caracazo was a wave of protests, rioting and looting that began on 27 February 1989 in Guarenas and Caracas, Venezuela, after President Carlos Andrés Pérez's austerity programme raised fuel prices and public transport fares.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/taif-agreement">Taif Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Taif Agreement was negotiated by Lebanese members of parliament at Taif in Saudi Arabia and signed in October 1989 to end the Lebanese Civil War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-the-berlin-wall">Fall of the Berlin Wall</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The fall of the Berlin Wall on the night of 9 November 1989 was the moment when East Germany, facing mass protests and the flight of its citizens to the West, opened the crossings through the wall that had divided Berlin since 1961.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-round-table-talks">Hungarian Round Table Talks</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hungarian Round Table Talks were negotiations held from June to September 1989 between the ruling communist party and the opposition.</p></div></li></ol></section>
