<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-panama"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Panama.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Panama</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States invades and removes Manuel Noriega</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/peoples-republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/People's%20Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>People's Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The army crushes the Tiananmen Square protests on 4 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/czechoslovakia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Czechoslovakia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Czechoslovakia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Velvet Revolution ends communist rule; Václav Havel becomes president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Estonia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Estonia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Baltic Way human chain links Tallinn, Riga and Vilnius</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The last Vietnamese troops withdraw from Cambodia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/liberia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Liberia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liberia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Charles Taylor’s invasion starts the first Liberian civil war</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/dictatorship"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dictatorship.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dictatorship</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Revolutions end the communist dictatorships of Central and Eastern Europe</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/sami"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/S%C3%A1mi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sámi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Sámi Parliament in Norway is elected, after Finland’s of 1973 and before Sweden’s of 1993</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hungary"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hungary.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hungary</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Hungarian Socialist Workers' Party opens Round Table Talks with the opposition in March; the reburial of Imre Nagy in June marks the symbolic end of communism in Hungary.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/lebanese-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lebanese%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lebanese Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Parliament agrees the Taif Agreement, with a timetable for Syrian withdrawal and equal Christian and Muslim representation; the war ends at the end of 1990.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/solidarity"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Solidarity.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Solidarity</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Round Table Talks lead to semi-free elections, and a Solidarity-led coalition government is formed under Tadeusz Mazowiecki</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/velvet-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Velvet%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Velvet Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Riot police attack a student march in Prague on International Students’ Day, and a false report that a student was killed spreads</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/velvet-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Velvet%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Velvet Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Civic Forum is founded in Prague and Public Against Violence in Bratislava</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/velvet-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Velvet%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Velvet Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Communist leadership resigns, a two-hour general strike is held and the Communist Party gives up its leading role</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/velvet-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Velvet%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Velvet Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">President Gustáv Husák appoints the first largely non-communist government since 1948, and Václav Havel is elected president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-arabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Arabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Arabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Arab Maghreb Union is formed in place of a proposed Algeria–Libya union</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/hindutva"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hindutva.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hindutva</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The BJP officially adopts Hindutva as its ideology in the Palampur resolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/peronism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Peronism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Peronism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Carlos Menem is elected president and turns to free-market policies and privatisation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/prague"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Velvet Revolution ends communist rule in Czechoslovakia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/sanchi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sanchi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sanchi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The monuments at Sanchi were listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/marxism-leninism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marxism%E2%80%93Leninism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marxism–Leninism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Revolts across Central and Eastern Europe bring down the Eastern Bloc governments, while China's government ends protests by force at Tiananmen Square</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/neoliberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Neoliberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Neoliberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Williamson sets out the ten rules later called the Washington Consensus</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Afghan mujahideen, with major support from the United States, force the Soviet Union from Afghanistan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/hittite-religion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hittite%20religion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hittite religion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Beckman observes that many Hittite towns maintained individual storm-gods</span></li></ul></section>
